Package: mica-mqtt-broker
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mica build <mica@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: micad (= @VERSION@), passwd, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: mica MQTT broker
 An rumqttd broker, TCP only and MQTT 3.1.1, listening on the address the
 device itself is configured with. The listen address, the port and the auth
 flag are deliberately absent from the unit: micad renders all three from the
 mqtt settings subtree into /run/mica/mqtt-broker.toml before starting it.
 .
 The dependency on micad is pinned to the exact version for that reason -- micad
 renders the only configuration this broker has and owns its lifecycle -- and
 the two are built from one workspace commit.
 .
 passwd is needed by the postinst, which creates the pinned mica-mqtt-broker
 service account with useradd, groupadd and chage. The uid is pinned rather
 than dynamic because /var/lib/mica/mqtt-broker-users.toml on STATE outlives
 every start of the unit and has to be owned by this service and nothing else.
 dpkg-shlibdeps cannot see a program that is exec'd by name, so the dependency
 is written out here.
 .
 The unit ships DISABLED: no multi-user.target.wants symlink is in this
 payload and nothing enables it. mqtt.enabled is the master switch and micad
 starts the broker from it.
